            rdf:value "Plant growth-promoting rhizobacteria (PGPR) are the rhizosphere bacteria that can enhance plant growth by a wide variety of mechanisms like phosphate solubilization, siderophore production, biological nitrogen fixation, rhizosphere engineering, production of 1-Aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate deaminase (ACC), quorum sensing (QS) signal interference and inhibition of biofilm formation, phytohormone production, exhibiting antifungal activity, production of volatile organic compounds (VOCs), induction of systemic resistance, promoting beneficial plant-microbe symbioses, interference with pathogen toxin production etc"@en ] ;
    skos:exactMatch agrovoc:c_cd313ffc,
        nalt:57623 ;
    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/eusoilvoc> ;
    skos:prefLabel "plant growth-promoting rhizobacteria"@en .

